      en: "The Aravan Petroglyphs in Aravan District, Osh Region, are rock carvings from the 2nd-1st millennium BCE. They depict animals such as ibex, horses, and deer, as well as hunting scenes. The engravings are on limestone cliffs at an altitude of 1,500 meters. They are part of the cultural heritage of Central Asian nomadic peoples. The site is relatively unexplored but of great archaeological significance. The petroglyphs are threatened by erosion. Since 2003, they have been under state protection.",
