      en: "Kyzyl-Tuu Heritage Village in Issyk-Kul District, Issyk-Kul Region, is a living museum of Kyrgyz nomadic culture. Founded in 2005, it preserves traditional crafts such as felt making, carpet weaving, and yurt construction. Visitors can tour yurts and participate in workshops. The village is on the southern shore of Lake Issyk-Kul. It also houses a small museum of historical artifacts. Kyzyl-Tuu is a model for sustainable cultural tourism in Kyrgyzstan.",
